\code{sigma2} uniform on (0, 1). Improvements can level off; mortality
increases cannot be forecast.
\item \code{core = "linear"}: \verb{rho[x, t] ~ N(b1[x] + b2[x] t, sigma^2)} with
\verb{(b1[x], b2[x])} bivariate normal with means \code{mu1}, \code{mu2} and covariance
from standard deviations \code{omega1}, \code{omega2} and correlation \code{r};
uniform priors \code{sigma}, \code{omega1}, \code{omega2} on (0, 1), \code{mu1}, \code{mu2} on
